<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seongjong of Goryeo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">961–997</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seongjong of Goryeo was king of Goryeo from 981 to 997. Following the advice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/choe-seung-ro">Choe Seung-ro</a>, he governed on Confucian principles, created twelve provincial governorships in 983 and founded the national academy, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gukjagam">Gukjagam</a>, in 992. In 993 he faced the first Khitan invasion, ended by the negotiations of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seo-hui">Seo Hui</a>.</p></div>
